From 27ad04265f553f09df606d9617a31d6e033c73c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:46:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/53] drm/imagination: bound JH7110 heap guards to VM
 lifetime

The downstream JH7110 workaround currently allocates and maps two 4 MiB
heap guards for every submit. The mappings persist until VM teardown, so
every submit leaks 8 MiB and consumes more GPU virtual address space.

Create the two mappings once per VM instead, serialize concurrent first
submissions, roll back partial setup, and fail submission if the required
workaround cannot be installed. Limit it to the exact JH7110 BVNC and make
the module parameter load-time only.

Install the guards before the deferred MMU flush so their page table
changes are visible to the first submitted job. Handle every VM present in
a multi-job submission rather than only the first one.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
